24: """Laptop OptiTrack -> calibrated base pose and immutable flight packets.
24: 
24: Chain:  Motive (NatNet UDP, cmd port 1510)  -->  motion_capture_tracking_node
24:         (vendored, namespace /optitrack; poses/tf remapped to /optitrack/*)
24:         --> optitrack_mct_relay --> /poses, /UCB_P1/pose, /UCB_P2/pose
24:         --> hope_ball_flight_packetizer --> /ball/flight_packet --> C++ Planner
24: 
24: Sibling of avatar_pro_hope_bridge.launch.py (ChingMu/VRPN backend); both emit
24: the identical HOPE topic contract, so everything downstream is unchanged.
24: The driver first applies motive_to_world from hope_world_frame.yaml to every
24: published world pose and point (body-local ModelDef coordinates stay local).
24: The default accepts the current named Motive body without a file hash or
24: marker-layout pin and assumes its identity marker-to-pelvis transform.
24: Use localization_source:=motive_asset for the optional pinned 17-marker check. Legacy
24: V2/V3 capture services are opt-in with localization_source:=calibration and
24: start_calibration:=true. It publishes the same schema-2 base-pose contract. In P2 table-side mode the relay rotates all
24: world poses 180 degrees about the table centre before Planner/base consumers.
24: The HDU transport relay republishes that Laptop-owned pose on the authoritative
24: Runner topic without recomputing calibration.
24: 
24: The remaps are LOAD-BEARING, not cosmetic:
24:   * the driver's `poses` topic is motion_capture_tracking_interfaces/
24:     NamedPoseArray -- on the bare /poses name it would collide with the HOPE
24:     /poses contract (geometry_msgs/PoseArray) as a DDS type mismatch;
24:   * the driver broadcasts /tf with raw body names (UCB_P1/PPT/...) which would
24:     fight the relay's world->UCB_P1/PPT transforms and the hope_world statics.
24: 
24: TODO before running on hardware (see docs/operations/run_mocap.md):
24:   * hostname -> the Motive PC IP on the arena LAN.
24:   * Motive streaming pane per mocap reference §6.3 (Z-up, Rigid Bodies ON,
24:     NatNet enabled; Multicast and Unicast are both supported and discovered
24:     from NAT_SERVERINFO). Labeled Markers is optional for asset identity verification; enable it
24:     to display the number of physically observed stickers.
24:   * rigid-body names + ball tracker are set in config/optitrack_mct.yaml and
24:     config/optitrack_relay.yaml (UCB_P1/UCB_P2/PPT assets; upstream ball
24:     'Ball' or 'ball', canonical downstream name 'Ball').
24:     The selected ``tracked_marker_frame`` overrides the marker aggregate's
24:     default UCB_P1 asset so P2 calibration receives UCB_P2 marker messages.
24:   * after verifying/importing the pelvis-aligned 17-station sticker asset, name it for
24:     the selected UCB frame, restart NatNet to refresh MODELDEF, and generate a
24:     fresh calibration/ucb_robot_to_pelvis.json receipt before policy entry.
24: """
24:                                                                          
24: 
24:                         ^
